# playwright, which tools/groundcheck.mjs and tools/build-icon.mjs both need and neither
# vendors — their own headers say "npm i playwright (not vendored)". It is installed outside
# the repo and symlinked in for the length of a session, so what lands here is a link to a
# path that exists on one machine. Ignored rather than deleted each time: it came back on
# every run, and an untracked entry that reappears is a thing to fix once, not to sweep.
# No trailing slash: it is a SYMLINK into the scratchpad, not a directory, and git treats a
# symlink as a file — "node_modules/" matched nothing and the entry kept showing up.
node_modules

# Scratch renders. The capture scripts write comparison sheets next to the app so a local
# server can reach them; none of it is the app.
_proof.html
